  ],
  "text": "Two people can agree a secret while shouting across a crowded room, and nobody else learns it. Which sounds impossible, because everything they said was heard by everyone. Start with a colour everybody can see. Both of them use the same one. Each secretly adds a colour of their own, and sends the mixture across the room. Then each adds their own secret colour again, to the mixture they received. Both now hold the identical colour, and nobody listening can make it. Because mixing paint is easy, and unmixing it is not. The real version uses numbers with the same property. Easy forwards, brutal backwards. Multiply two huge primes and it is instant. Work out which two, and you can be there for centuries. Which is why a big enough quantum computer would matter. Some of that unmixing gets easy. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
